# What this file is for: the diffs GitHub shows for this repository, and the
# language it reports.
#
# Measured, before any of the rules below (tracked bytes):
#
#   Go              1,372,484   181 files
#   YAML              298,635    44
#   Markdown          234,874    37
#   go.sum             45,496     1
#   Go Template        30,279     9
#
# The label is already right: GitHub reports Go, and Go is 97% of the bytes
# it counts. So unlike a repository whose language is wrong, almost nothing
# here is about the language bar — it is about the DIFF. A file nobody reads
# line by line should arrive collapsed, or it buries the change somebody does
# have to read.
#
# The two attributes do different things, which decides most of what is below:
# linguist-generated excludes from stats AND hides in diffs, while
# linguist-vendored only excludes from stats.

# ─── Generated: the module checksum file ─────────────────────────────────
# 45 KB of resolver output, reviewed as "the lock moved" and never line by
# line. It is the one rule here with a measurable effect on review.
#
# Not redundant, checked in Linguist's own generated.rb rather than assumed:
# that file knows Gopkg.lock, glide.lock, poetry.lock, pdm.lock, uv.lock,
# pixi.lock and the JavaScript lockfiles, and go.sum is not among them.
#
# go.mod is deliberately absent. It is hand-edited — it carries an `exclude`
# with the reason a dependency is held back — and collapsing it would hide
# exactly the line a reviewer needs to see.
go.sum linguist-generated=true

# ─── Not this repository's language ──────────────────────────────────────
# A Homebrew bundle, which Linguist reads as Ruby because languages.yml claims
# the filename. It is ALL of the Ruby GitHub reports — 4,944 bytes — for a
# repository that contains none.
#
# `-linguist-detectable` rather than -generated or -vendored, because both of
# those would be untrue: it is hand-written and a reviewer should see it in
# full. The attribute says only "do not count this as a language".
Brewfile -linguist-detectable

# ─── Deliberately not marked ─────────────────────────────────────────────
# The vendored upstream manifest,
# layers/30-cluster-services/manifests/kubelet-serving-cert-approver.yaml.
# linguist-vendored would do nothing for it: YAML is a `data` language, so it
# never reaches the language bar anyway, and vendored does not touch diffs.
# linguist-generated would collapse it, which is the opposite of what the
# layer's own comment asks for — the copy is committed so that "the diff is
# reviewable", and internal/ci refuses an edit to it by digest.
#
# `.github/**` needs no rule: Linguist's vendor.yml already matches it. That
# is why .github/commit-type.awk is absent from the reported Awk and
# tools/lines/main.awk is all 5,756 bytes of it.
#
# internal/pkg/charts/*.yaml.tmpl stay detectable on purpose. The Helm values
# templates are written and reviewed here, and "Go Template" describes them
# honestly.
#
# The five .task/remote/*.checksum files are machine-written and no reviewer
# can verify a sha256 by eye, but they are 320 bytes in total — collapsing
# five short lines is not worth a rule.
